    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p10-problem-2-short-pairwise",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Adding the three set sizes counts each region in exactly two sets twice. Subtracting the pairwise intersections reduces that count to one.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p10-problem-2-short-triple",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The centre was added three times and subtracted three times. Add the triple intersection once so every element in the union is counted once.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Label the numbers of elements in the three set-only regions $a$, $b$ and $c$. Label the numbers in the $AB$-only, $AC$-only and $BC$-only overlaps $d$, $e$ and $f$ respectively. Label the number in the centre $g$.\n\nAdding $\\lvert A\\rvert+\\lvert B\\rvert+\\lvert C\\rvert$ counts $a$, $b$ and $c$ once each, $d$, $e$ and $f$ twice each, and $g$ three times.\n\nEach pairwise intersection contains its pairwise-only region and the centre. Subtracting their sizes removes one copy each of $d$, $e$ and $f$, and all three copies of $g$. Add $\\lvert A\\cap B\\cap C\\rvert$ to restore one copy of $g$. Each region in the union is now counted exactly once.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\lvert A\\cup B\\cup C\\rvert&=\\lvert A\\rvert+\\lvert B\\rvert+\\lvert C\\rvert-\\lvert A\\cap B\\rvert-\\lvert A\\cap C\\rvert-\\lvert B\\cap C\\rvert+\\lvert A\\cap B\\cap C\\rvert\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": [
